# WARNING -- THIS FILE'S BOUNDS ARE INCOMPLETE. See roadmap 6.18. (2026-07-13)
# =============================================================================
# requirements.lock is compiled from THIS file, and because two of the ranges above have NO
# UPPER BOUND, pip-compile resolves them to versions that are KNOWN TO BREAK THIS PROJECT:
#
#   transformers>=4.40   -> resolves to 5.8.0. The transformers 5.x family KILLED a Run 17
#                           smoke test: the Nucleotide Transformer fetches head-of-main remote
#                           code that imports a symbol transformers 5.x removed. The working
#                           pin is 4.46.3 (see requirements.txt).
#   pandas>=2.0          -> unbounded. pandas 3.0.4's Windows cp312 wheel segfaults
#                           pd.date_range (0xC0000005). The working pin is 2.3.3.
#
# requirements.lock is therefore a TRAP: it is installed by nothing today, and installing it
# would re-introduce a break the project already paid to escape. Both ceilings must be added
# here, the lock recompiled UNDER PYTHON 3.12, and the result verified to reproduce the
# known-good stack EXACTLY, before requirements.lock can become the single install target.
# That is roadmap 6.18 -- a deliberate, separately-verified change.